# Copy to .env for local development:  cp .env.example .env
#
# `shopify app dev` injects SHOPIFY_API_KEY, SHOPIFY_API_SECRET, SCOPES and
# SHOPIFY_APP_URL itself, so the only variable you must set by hand is the
# database. In production every one of these is set on the host instead (see
# docs/DEPLOYMENT.md) and this file is never deployed.

# Postgres, in local development as well as production. Prisma migrations are
# provider-specific SQL, so a second provider for local dev means a second
# migration history and the two drift apart - which is how the deployed branch
# ended up four commits behind with a retired API version.
#
# Create a free database at https://neon.tech, then use a SEPARATE branch from
# the production one so development never writes to live merchant data.
# Use the POOLED host and keep ?sslmode=require.
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@ep-xxxx-pooler.REGION.aws.neon.tech/neondb?sslmode=require"

# Only needed when testing against a store on a custom domain.
# SHOP_CUSTOM_DOMAIN=

# Set to 1 to exercise the billing screens with test charges that never bill.
# SHOPIFY_BILLING_TEST=1
